body:
I'm seing an issue in tests because the channel is not yet initialized on registration, i.e the code:

```
        b.handler(new ChannelInitializer<DatagramChannel>() {
            @Override
            protected void initChannel(DatagramChannel ch) throws Exception {
                ch.pipeline().addLast(DECODER, ENCODER, responseHandler);
            }
        });
b.option(ChannelOption.DATAGRAM_CHANNEL_ACTIVE_ON_REGISTRATION, true);

ChannelFuture channelFuture = b.register();
```

does not guarantee that the `initChannel` is invoked when the `channelFuture` is succeeded. As consequence sometimes during tests the `DatagramDnsQuery` are not encoded as the `ENCODER` is not yet added to the pipeline.

One solution is to use a promise that is resolved after the pipeline has been modified instead of using the channelFuture.

Thoughts ?
